{#- ======================================================================
    Info sheet template (Jinja2). Edit freely.
    Silhouette Studio interface labels (FRENCH UI) are collected here so
    they can be corrected in one place.  >>> PLEASE CONFIRM THESE <<<
    ====================================================================== -#}
{%- set studio = {
  "file_menu":        "Fichier",
  "open":             "Ouvrir…",
  "merge":            "Fusionner…",
  "page_setup":       "Configuration de la page",
  "page_size":        "Format de page",
  "letter":           "Lettre",
  "reg_marks":        "Repères d'enregistrement",
  "mark_style":       "Style",
  "type1":            "Type 1",
  "inset":            "Retrait",
  "length":           "Longueur",
  "thickness":        "Épaisseur",
  "transform":        "Transformer",
  "position":         "Position",
  "send":             "Envoyer",
  "material":         "Matériau",
  "action_cut":       "Couper",
  "blade_depth":      "Profondeur de lame",
  "force":            "Force",
  "test_cut":         "Test de découpe",
} -%}
PRODUCTION INFO SHEET
=====================
{{ title }}
Generated {{ generated }}
Orders: {{ orders | join(", ") }}

{% for f in finishes -%}
-------------------------------------------------------------------
FINISH: {{ f.label }}  ({{ f.sheets }} sheet{{ "s" if f.sheets != 1 }}, {{ f.labels }} labels)
Media: {{ f.media }}    Laminate: {{ f.laminate }}
Print file: {{ f.pdf }}
{% if f.notch %}Laminate notch file: {{ notch_dxf }}  (place at X 0 mm, Y 0 mm)
{% endif %}
  Page | Labels | Cut file (DXF)                       |     X mm |     Y mm |     W mm |     H mm
{% for p in f.pages -%}
  {{ "%4d"|format(p.n) }} | {{ "%6d"|format(p.count) }} | {{ "%-36s"|format(p.dxf) }} | {{ "%8.2f"|format(p.x) }} | {{ "%8.2f"|format(p.y) }} | {{ "%8.2f"|format(p.w) }} | {{ "%8.2f"|format(p.h) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor -%}
-------------------------------------------------------------------
SILHOUETTE STUDIO SET-UP (once)
  • {{ studio.page_setup }} → {{ studio.page_size }}: {{ studio.letter }} (215.9 × 279.4 mm), portrait.
  • {{ studio.reg_marks }}: on, {{ studio.mark_style }} = {{ studio.type1 }},
    {{ studio.inset }} {{ mark_inset }} mm, {{ studio.length }} {{ mark_length }} mm, {{ studio.thickness }} {{ mark_thickness }} mm.

PRODUCTION STEPS (for each sheet)
  1. Print the page at 100 % (actual size, no "fit to page"), one sheet at a time.
  2. Let the ink dry, ideally overnight (dye ink).
  3. Laminate the sheet.{% if any_notch %} For {{ notch_finishes | join(" and ") }}: notch the laminate
     first — cut the three {{ notch }} × {{ notch }} mm corner squares off the laminate
     ({{ notch_dxf }}) so the Cameo can read the marks.{% endif %}
  4. Load the sheet on the mat. In Silhouette Studio: {{ studio.file_menu }} → {{ studio.merge }}
     the page's cut file (DXF), then in {{ studio.transform }} → {{ studio.position }}
     type the X and Y from the table above. Check W and H match.
  5. {{ studio.send }}: kiss cut through the laminate and vinyl, not the backing
     (adjust {{ studio.blade_depth }} / {{ studio.force }}; do a {{ studio.test_cut }} on a new roll).
